nt of the Group’s land bank locally and abroad. More recently, Berjaya Property Berhad has begun to create a growing presence abroad particularly in Japan, Korea, Vietnam and China. In essence, Berjaya not only offers homes of brick and mortar but more importantly, the company creates beautiful lifestyles and successful residential developments.\n\n### Contact Us\n\n  * +6011-1722 5515\n\n  * Level 12, East, Berjaya Times Square, No. 1, Jalan Imbi, 55100 Kuala Lumpur\n\n  * property@berjaya.com.my\n\nCopyright © 2024. All Rights Reserved | BERJAYA PROPERTY BERHAD (Formerly known as Berjaya Land Berhad) 199001010193 (201765-A)--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.berjayaproperties.com/development)\nciteturn279search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; The Tropika Bukit Jalil ... Berjaya Properties Berjaya Property Berhad is one of the prominent property developers in Malaysia, responsible for some of Malaysia’s most sought-after developments. ...   * property@berjaya.com.my\n\n## Our Development\n\n# PROPERTY SEARCH\n\nLOCATION [Select] STATUS [Select]\n\nBayu Timur Residences\n\n\nJesselton Courtyard at Jesselton Selatan\n\nPangsapuri Azalea\n\nTimes Square 2\n\nThe Tropika Bukit Jalil\n\nThe Ritz-Carlton Residences Kuala Lumpur\n\nThe Peak\n\nBerjaya Hills\n\nKensington Gardens\n\nSeputeh Heights\n\nThe Link 2\n\nLanai Residences\n\n## The Tropika\nBukit Jalil\n\n#### LIFESTYLE AT YOUR CONVENIENCE\n\nStrategically located at Bukit Jalil, The Tropika is a unique nature-inspired mixed development and lifestyle hotspot comprising of residential and commercial components that combines community living with city conveniences.\n\nImage\n\n## The Ritz-Carlton Residences Kuala Lumpur\n\n#### A HERITAGE OF LUXURY LIVING\n\nThe Ritz-Carlton Residences, Kuala Lumpur, Jalan Sultan Ismail, are designed to be the hallmark of luxury living, with the legendary service and impeccable attention to detail. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://mail.berjayaproperties.com/news-details-the-tropika)\nciteturn279search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.7 years ago; Crawled: 3 days ago; Occupying a 2.6ha freehold parcel, The Tropika has a total of 868 apartment units spread across four towers, with four types of specially designed units. ... The units range from 732 sq ft (two-bedroom) to 1,318 sq ft (three-bedroom). ... Call Berjaya Property Gallery at 603-8994 4866 or visit https://berjayaproperties.com/project/the-tropika for more information on the available units.\n\n## News & Events\n\nJanuary 15, 2021\n\nSharen Kaur\n\n### The Tropika @ Bukit Jalil selling well despite the on-going pandemic\n\nBerjaya Land (BLand) Berhad's nature-inspired mixed development in Bukit Jalil called The Tropika is selling very well in spite of the on-going pandemic and slow economy.\nThe RM781 million project, developed by Berjaya Hartanah Berhad, a subsidiary of BLand, the pioneer developer in Bukit Jalil offers modern amenities nestled amid lush greenery, and this makes it one of the few developments in Klang Valley which such an unique and natural offering.\nSome units at the gated and guarded residence overlook the Bukit Jalil Golf & Country Resort.\nOccupying a 2.6ha freehold parcel, The Tropika has a total of 868 apartment units spread across four towers, with four types of specially designed units. There are Type A, Type B, Type C, and Type D units measuring 732 sq ft, 974 sq ft, 1318 sq ft, and 1251 sq ft respectively, offering an easy entry point for middle-income home buyers.\n\nImage\n\nType A unit. Courtesy image\n\nSo far BLand has launched Tower A and Tower B and both have garnered significant sales. Tower A with 229 units was launched February 23, 2019, and recorded a 65 per cent take-up back then. The units range from 732 sq ft (two-bedroom) to 1,318 sq ft (three-bedroom).\nThe launch price starts from RM575,800 for the smaller units to as high as RM1.03 million for the bigger apartments. The price, which is at an average of RM720 psf is considered reasonable compared with projects by other developers in the neighbourhood that offer less in their developments.\nThe most pleasant part about The Tropika is that there are only five to seven units per level, providing privacy to the residents.\nThe project has a commercial component making it a valuable and complete development for the residents. The commercial space comprises a 23,695 sq ft grocer (Jaya Grocer), two-storey dual frontage shop office ranging from 3,316 sq ft to 3,814 sq ft, and retail space ranging from 752 sq ft to 1,677 sq ft.\nAnother interesting feature which is attracting home buyers to The Tropika is the unique 1.17ha full-fledged deck that comes with 68 types of facilities grouped under eight lifestyle categories that you see in no other development.\nOne of the best landscape feature on the deck is its biophilic design, which is a rare sight in other projects as the investment is a lot. The biophilic design focuses on connecting a building's occupants with nature. The deck will resemble a forest canopy where the uppermost branches of the trees avoid touching one another — a phenomenon known as crown shyness — thereby creating channel-like gaps.\nThe other facilities include an infinity swimming pool, indoor and outdoor gymnasiums, a dance studio and boxing ring, a zen garden, a rock-climbing wall, camping grounds, and an e-charging station, giving all the privilege to the residents to enjoy various lifestyle activities in a tranquil environment under one roof.\nBerjaya Land Bhd chief executive officer Syed Ali Shahul Hameed said The Tropika has attracted young families and the millennial generation. Courtesy image\n\nSuccessful take-up and price appreciation\nBLand chief executive officer Syed Ali Shahul Hameed told NST Property that The Tropika has attracted young families and the millennial generation.\nSyed Ali said it aims to launch Tower C in April and Tower D at the end of this year, depending on the market situation and the pandemic.\nThe launch price for Tower C range from RM732,800 to RM1.314 million, while Tower D is between RM779,800 and RM1.391 million, he said.\n\"We develop innovative products and comfortable living spaces that cater for multi-generations. The Tropika provides residents with a sense of urban living amid lush greenery. Residents can live at a leisurely pace within this sanctuary,\" he said.\nSyed Ali said Bukit Jalil is still one of the most sought-after neighbourhoods in Kuala Lumpur by owner-occupiers and investors as they see great growth potential in the area.\nHe said despite the on-going pandemic, there is an influx of interest from home-seekers and investors looking for a safe haven.\nToday in the market the units, which were completed in 2016 are worth RM770,000 to RM1.52 million.\n\nImage\n\nKM1 West, comprising 350 units was completed in 2014. The units, ranging from 1,335 sq ft to 1,508 sq ft sold at RM450 psf, and the market price today is between RM830,000 and RM1 million.\n\"All the properties have done very well. If you bought a unit in Bukit Jalil 10 to 20 years ago, you would be doing very well today. There is a fairly nice increment in selling price and rental despite market uncertainties,\" Syed Ali said.\nSyed Ali expects The Tropika to also have a fair increment in selling price in the secondary market.\nThe Tropika is slated for completion in February 2023 while the commercial development is expected to be completed by December this year, with Jaya Grocer commencing operations next year.\nBLand still has around 5ha of undeveloped land bank in Bukit Jalil and there is a plan to develop an RM2 billion healthcare hub on it. If the healthcare plan materialises soon, it will complement the overall development, setting a new pricing benchmark.\nStrategic location\nThe Tropika is located opposite the Bukit Jalil Golf & Country Resort and next to the Link 2.\nThere is easy access from the project to major highways such as the Damansara-Puchong Expressway (LDP), Puchong-Sungai Besi Highway, Shah Alam Expressway, Maju Expressway (MEX), and New Pantai Expressway.\nThe Tropika is also well-served by public transportation, including the Rapid KL bus and Light Rail Transit train services.\nIt is also within close proximity to various established educational institutions such as SJKC Lai Meng, International Medical University, and Asia Pacific University, as well as sporting and recreational facilities such as the Bukit Jalil Complex, the Bukit Jalil Recreational Park, and the Bukit Jalil Golf & Country Resort.\nCall Berjaya Property Gallery at 603-8994 4866 or visit https://berjayaproperties.com/project/the-tropika for more information on the available units.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAnother Prestigious Project By: (https://berjayaproperties.com/storage/The_Tropika_Bukit_Jalil_Brochure.pdf)\nciteturn279search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.5 years ago; W : berjayaproperties.com.my ... T : 03-8994 4866 ... Pelan Bangunan: BP 3S OSC 2018 1791 • Pajakan Tanah: Pegangan Kekal • Cagaran: RHB Bank Berhad • Tarikh Dijangka Siap: Feb 2023 • Jenis Hartanah: Residen Servis • Jumlah Unit: 868 unit • Diskaun Bumiputera: 5% • Harga Jualan: Blok A (Min.: RM575,800 – Maks.: RM1,028,800), Blok B (Min.: RM617,800 – Maks.: RM1,391,800), Blok C (Min.: RM732,800 – Maks.: RM1,314,800), Blok D (Min.: RM779,800 – Maks.: RM1,391,800).\nAnother Prestigious Project By:\n\nBERJAYA\n\nDeveloper:\nBerjaya Hartanah Berhad\n(Formerly known as Berjaya Golf Resort Berhad) (Company No.:223292-U)\n(A subsidiary of Berjaya Land Berhad - Company No.:201765-A)\n\nHead Office:\nLevel 12, East, Berjaya Times Square,\nNo. 1, Jalan Imbi 55100 Kuala Lumpur.\nT : 03-2142 8028\nF : 03-2143 2028\nE : property@berjaya.com.my\nW : berjayaproperties.com.my\n\nProperty Gallery:\nBerjaya Property Gallery Bukit Jalil\nLot 36471, Jalan Jalil Perkasa 7,\nBukit Jalil, 57100 Kuala Lumpur.\nT : 03-8994 4866\n: Berjaya Property Gallery Bukit Jalil\n\n• No. Lesen Pemaju: 5660-13/01-2022/01079(L) • Tempoh Sah Lesen: 21/01/2021 - 20/01/2022 • No. Lesen Permit: 5660-13/01-2022/01079(P) • Tempoh Sah Lesen: 21/01/2021 - 20/01/2022 • Pihak Berkuasa Yang Meluluskan Pelan Bangunan: Dewan Bandaraya Kuala Lumpur • No. Pelan Bangunan: BP 3S OSC 2018 1791 • Pajakan Tanah: Pegangan Kekal • Cagaran: RHB Bank Berhad • Tarikh Dijangka Siap: Feb 2023 • Jenis Hartanah: Residen Servis • Jumlah Unit: 868 unit • Diskaun Bumiputera: 5% • Harga Jualan: Blok A (Min.: RM575,800 – Maks.: RM1,028,800), Blok B (Min.: RM617,800 – Maks.: RM1,391,800), Blok C (Min.: RM732,800 – Maks.: RM1,314,800), Blok D (Min.: RM779,800 – Maks.: RM1,391,800). All art renderings and pictures in this brochure are artist’s impressions only. While every care is taken in providing this information, any inaccuracy and/or omission is not intentional. The developer cannot be held responsible for variations without notifications as may be required by the relevant authorities or developer’s architect and cannot form part of an offer or contract.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.berjayaproperties.com/news-details-bland-expand)\nciteturn279search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.1 years ago; Crawled: last week; Its latest project, The Tropika, boasts a contemporary concept that suits the tastebuds of the millennial generation ENVISAGED to be the next Bukit Jalil lifestyle hub with community living at the fore, The Tropika is poised to rekindle Berjaya Land Berhad's past glory as the pioneer developer in Bukit Jalil. ... With a total of 868 residential units spread across four towers, the project which is due for completion in 2023 offers a golf course view alongside retail units on a 6.5-acre freehold parcel. ... The built-ups range from 732 to 1,318 sq ft with the price per sq ft being in excess of RM720. ... Additionally, there are also several Light Rail Transit stations within a 3km radius of the project site (notably the Awan Besar, Sri Petaling and Bukit Jalil stations).\n\n## News & Events\n\nSeptember 07, 2019\n\nSharen Kaur\n\n### Berjaya Land expands footprint in Bukit Jalil\n\nIts latest project, The Tropika, boasts a contemporary concept that suits the tastebuds of the millennial generation ENVISAGED to be the next Bukit Jalil lifestyle hub with community living at the fore, The Tropika is poised to rekindle Berjaya Land Berhad's past glory as the pioneer developer in Bukit Jalil.\nInterestingly, the gated and guarded high-rise residential project will be undertaken by Berjaya Golf Resort Berhad, the Berjaya Land Berhad subsidiary which constructed the famous 18-hole Bukit Jalil Golf and Country Resort decades ago.\nBerjaya Land Berhad has thus far played an instrumental role in the transformation of Bukit Jalil, which is renowned for hosting the 1998 Commonwealth Games, as a real estate hotspot vis-à-vis its array of bungalows and high-rise developments such as Savanna and Savanna 2, Covillea, KM1 East and West, Greenfields, Green Avenue and The Link 2 Residences.\nWith a total of 868 residential units spread across four towers, the project which is due for completion in 2023 offers a golf course view alongside retail units on a 6.5-acre freehold parcel. Its gross development value stands at RM780 mil.\nThe built-ups range from 732 to 1,318 sq ft with the price per sq ft being in excess of RM720. The selling price starts from RM575,800. There are seven units per floor served by four lifts. All units come with two parking bays each.\n\"We expect to launch Tower B once Tower A hits 80% sales,\" enthuses Berjaya Land CEO Syed Ali Shahul Hameed. \"Sales have been brisk especially since we rolled out HouzKey, a home financing solution between Berjaya Land Berhad and Maybank Islamic Bhd which is specially made available for home buyers of The Tropika.\"\nUnder the HouzKey scheme, home buyers get to enjoy easy entry by having to pay only three months of security deposit upfront. This is suited for first-time home buyers and upgraders who are eager to own a home without worrying about the upfront cost.\n\"The Tropika stands out as the first project in Bukit Jalil to introduce HouzKey,\" Syed Ali points out. \"Above all else, HouzKey offers greater flexibility and better cash flow as home buyers can opt to stay first before deciding to purchase the property within five years.\"\nMultiple conveniences\nA unique selling proposition of The Tropika which makes it stand out from other high-rise projects in the vicinity is perhaps the blending of lifestyle conveniences into its architecture and landscaping aspects - a feature that is very much sought by its target purchasers comprising young families and the millennial generation (those in the 30s to 40s age group).\nUnderstanding the preference of the younger generation who prefers community living with lifestyle conveniences, The Tropika has in the pipeline neighbourhood mixed retail shops with Jaya Grocer as the anchor tenant.\nBerjaya Land Berhad, through Berjaya Golf Resort Berhad, recently inked a lease agreement with Trendcell Sdn Bhd to operate a Jaya Grocer outlet which will take up 23,695 sq ft of commercial space in about two-and-a-half years' time.\n\"Having a grocer at one's doorstep is deemed to benefit a property development in the long run given it spells convenience to residents who may prefer to touch and feel fresh produce (fruits and vegetables) as opposed to ordering them from online grocers,\" justifies Syed Ali.\n\"That The Tropika has been chosen to house a Jaya Grocer store speaks volumes of its premier location (within Bukit Jalil) and its ability to extend such convenience to the surrounding Bukit Jalil community.\" Besides Jaya Grocer, the commercial component of The Tropika will also feature double-storey dual-frontage office lots with built-ups ranging from 3,316 to 3,814 sq ft, nine double-storey dual-frontage shops with built-ups ranging from 3,316 to 3,814 sq ft while the retail lots will have built-ups of 752 to 1,677 sq ft.\n\"In this regard, we hope to lease out the retail spaces to restaurants, gyms, and pharmacies, among others,\" says Syed Ali. \"By so doing, we can add value to the homes in The Tropika by ensuring most of the basic conveniences are within reach.\"\nGiven that most purchasers are likely to have young children, the developer has also thoughtfully incorporated 68 facilities which can be grouped under eight lifestyle categories. These are housed within the 2.9-acre facilities podium to create a vibrant and interactive community among residents.\nElsewhere, the Bukit Jalil sports complex which comprises the national stadium (the largest stadium in the country and the second largest in Southeast Asia), the Putra Indoor Stadium (now renamed Axiata Arena), National Aquatic Centre and the National Hockey Stadium are within the neighbourhood.\n\"With the many sporting hubs in its vicinity, Bukit Jalil is indeed a perfect location for fitness enthusiasts,\" observes Tan.\nMoreover, there are a number of upcoming new developments/enhancements that will contribute to the positive growth of Bukit Jalil in the near future. Among them are the Pavillion Bukit Jalil, the new International Medical University Hospital (first private hospital in Bukit Jalil), the Tzu Chi International School and the upgrading of the existing Bukit Jalil Highway.\nConnectivity-wise, The Tropika is accessible via major highways such as the Shah Alam Expressway, Bukit Jalil Highway, Maju Expressway, KL-Seremban Highway and the Kuala Lumpur Middle Ring Road 2.\nAdditionally, there are also several Light Rail Transit stations within a 3km radius of the project site (notably the Awan Besar, Sri Petaling and Bukit Jalil stations).\nIn allaying concerns over a property glut in Bukit Jalil which in turn may result in value stagnation, Tan opines that there is still a limited number of high-rise developments in Bukit Jalil on the bigger picture.\nCiting property consultant and research firm Rahim & Co International Sdn Bhd, he says property prices in Bukit Jalil are still holding up despite the current soft property market compared to some other locations in the Klang Valley.\n\"Besides that, there's already limited land parcel available along Jalan Jalil Perkasa 1 for future high-rise development as most of the land is occupied by the Bukit Jalil recreational park and Bukit Jalil golf course,\" he adds.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTYPE A\n\n2 BEDROOMS  \n2 BATHS\n\nTOTAL BUILT-UP  \n732 (https://www.berjayaproperties.com/storage/The_Tropika_Bukit_Jalil_Brochure.pdf)\nciteturn279search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.5 years ago; 732 sq. ft.\nTYPE A\n\n2 BEDROOMS  \n2 BATHS\n\nTOTAL BUILT-UP  \n732 sq. ft.\n\nTower layout diagram for Type A shows Towers A, B, C, and D with unit stacks labeled A, B, C, and D; highlighted units are shown in gold.\n\nFloor plan dimensions and labels for Type A:\n- 8200 (horizontal span)\n- 10200 (vertical span)\n\nRoom labels in Type A floor plan:\n- LIVING\n- MASTER BEDROOM\n- MASTER BATH\n- BEDROOM 2\n- DINING\n- BATH 2\n- KITCHEN\n- YARD\n- A/C LEDGE\n\nTYPE B\n\n3 BEDROOMS  \n3 BATHS\n\nTOTAL BUILT-UP  \n974 sq. ft.\n\nTower layout diagram for Type B shows Towers A, B, C, and D with unit stacks labeled A, B, C, and D; highlighted units are shown in gold.\n\nFloor plan dimensions and labels for Type B:\n- 11525 (horizontal span)\n- 10200 (vertical span)\n\nRoom labels in Type B floor plan:\n- MASTER BEDROOM\n- MASTER BATH\n- LIVING\n- BEDROOM 2\n- BEDROOM 3\n- BATH 2\n- BATH 3\n- DINING\n- KITCHEN\n- YARD\n- A/C LEDGE--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFreehold Residences (https://www.berjayaproperties.com/storage/The_Tropika_Bukit